<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Appalachian Spring (Aaron Copland)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1944</span><span class="sg-chain-h">melody used in the ballet score</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Old American Songs (Aaron Copland)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1950</span><span class="sg-chain-h">arrangement for voice and piano</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lord of the Dance (Sydney Carter)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1963</span><span class="sg-chain-h">tune and words adapted as a hymn</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Too Young to Be One (The Turtles)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1967</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted by Eric Eisner</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Chorale and Shaker Dance (John P. Zdechlik)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1972</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used in a work for concert band</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lord of the Dance (Michael Flatley)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1996</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Carter's hymn adapted by Ronan Hardiman for the show</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Greatest Man That Ever Lived (Weezer)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">melody used throughout</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Sound Above My Hair (Scooter)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2009</span><span class="sg-chain-h">central melody used</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Air and Simple Gifts (John Williams)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2009</span><span class="sg-chain-h">variation for the inauguration of Barack Obama</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Simple Gifts: Four Shaker Songs (Frank Ticheli)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">variation</span></li></ul></section>
